PRE applies a negative impulse, giving the opposite raw response. The author's nonnegative strength is the negative sum of its two raw slopes and therefore equals the PRE's positive sum. There is no sign repair to make. The factors of one half in both quadratures are also identical; using unnormalized quadratures for both kick and readout would multiply the strengths by four.

