K cancels from this ratio within the conditional model. That algebra does not identify the response probe or original marks with measured optical quantities.

For definite initial number \(N_0\), h and \(\Gamma\) commute with N, hence every no-event propagator preserves that number sector. Each original resolved or stipulated coherent jump raises number by two. A history Kraus operator with r marks maps the initial sector into \(N_0+2r\), or annihilates it. Whenever the conditional state is defined with nonzero history weight, it therefore has
