The history statement is about this aggregate bounded observable, not a field state or energy law fixed by r. For an initial number mixture or number coherences, posterior weights can change under conditioning; the author correctly withholds that fixed-\(N_0\) replacement while retaining the unconditional balance.

On the fourth-moment initial class, the graph bounds also preserve that moment on each finite history with nonzero weight. Outside that class the author's history formula remains a bounded-observable statement; PRE supplies the stronger general-normal response interpretation if explicitly adopted later.

